    "created_at": "2016-03-07T15:07:46Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-07T15:07:46Z",
    "body": "Not really since it only refers to frame rates. And as written it implies trying to achieve a smooth frame rate. And obviously Chrome has been able to create an incompatible timer/raf callback sequence per the test case I provided. Run it a few times and you'll see the raf and timeout 2 swap places. \n\nI think without clearly specifying timer behavior you can't use the prose to write interoperable behavior.\n\nBasically nothing says - look at the remaining tasks in each queue and determine if there is a task which should run before updating the rendering, in which case remove that document from the list and/or abort these steps. \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
