    "created_at": "2016-03-07T15:19:40Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-07T15:19:40Z",
    "body": "Well, the frame rates thing is only an example of why you might remove the document from the list. It's pretty clear that \"This specification does not mandate any particular model for when to update the rendering.\"\n\nAnd I think in general it would be a better strategy to coalesce timers only in the 16.666 milliseconds between frames; if timer-coalescing would break your 60fps performance, then you should avoid coalescing for that frame. But maybe that's my Blink engineer talking.\n\nIn general I don't think we're going to achieve complete interop on these questions since an important part of user-agent engineering is making smart decisions on when to update the rendering.\n\nBut, if you think that the example there isn't enough to support the kind of decisions on when to update the rendering that Edge prefers, we can certainly expand it to not only talk about maintaining frame rates, but also about looking at other tasks in the queue that you might want to run in sequence without updating the rendering in between them. Let me know and I'll work on a PR for that.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
