    "created_at": "2016-03-07T15:39:47Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-03-07T15:39:47Z",
    "body": "I think having one additional step that implies we can filter would be nice. Also I think if you are spinning the event loop then rendering may be blocked. Basically when one type of task is blocked and the rendering is not ready. Maybe that is already accounted though with some of the other reasons about active documents. \n\nWe have had bugs where not coalescing timers and favoring them over paints has led to bugs as noted. These are very hard to track down. I'm surprised that the Chrome devs haven't seen these issues yet. We get them 2-3 times a year around some subtle timer, event, input, paint series. \n\nNote that Edge achieves 60fps separately from the UI thread as well which is different from 60fps of the main event loop. This is why we favor the author work so much. It often leads to differences in our page load times. Generally we find on fast hardware that we load faster but paint later than other browsers. Which gives the opposite on perceived perf. Independent rendering was meant to fix that but often something causes us to fail candidacy and we are also still synchronous until we have a paintable sync point. \n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
